WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.697
The important question is whether the join preserves the measure's fact grain.

00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:08.927
A many-to-one lookup often preserves the fact rows.

00:00:08.927 --> 00:00:13.747
A broad join between two fact-like tables can multiply them.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:20.172
If rows are already duplicated before the pivot, the pivot aggregates inflated facts.

00:00:20.172 --> 00:00:23.802
Check row counts and key relationships first.

00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:28.607
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:28.607 --> 00:00:34.082
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain before

00:00:34.082 --> 00:00:42.160
combining them. This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
